# A flashed-back Esper Origins that is countered never resolves, so none of its text happens: no surveil, no life, and
# it is not put onto the battlefield. Flashback exiles it as it leaves the stack (CR 702.34a, the ruling: "whether it
# resolves, is countered, or leaves the stack in some other way"), so it ends in exile, front face up, and not in the
# graveyard to be flashed back again. Bot1's life stays at 22 from the turn-1 cast from hand.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Emerald
Mox Jet
Esper Origins
Forest x3
Forest
Lightning Bolt
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Counterspell
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Esper Origins.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Forest; Lightning Bolt |)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Island.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Graveyard.Esper Origins.Cast(Ability: Flashback)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Counterspell.Cast(Stack.Esper Origins)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Exile = Esper Origins
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield = Forest; Forest; Mox Emerald; Mox Jet
Bot1.Life = 22
Bot1.Library = Lightning Bolt; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest; Forest
Bot2.Graveyard = Counterspell
